        "heading": "How ministerial offices are constituted",
        "content": "A ministry is an executive portfolio with a legally defined remit. Under Article 133 of Iran's constitution, the president nominates ministers for parliamentary confidence; legislation determines their number and powers. Article 134 assigns cabinet coordination to the president. These provisions establish formal responsibilities rather than demonstrating how effectively departments cooperate. [s1]",
