        "content": "Iran's ministerial terminology contains distinctions that can be unfamiliar to international readers. The Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Science, Research and Technology are separate portfolios. Health is combined with medical education in another ministry. Petroleum and Energy also appear separately, as do Cultural Guidance and Foreign Affairs. The Iran Data Portal's directory illustrates these distinctions, but its undated list should not be treated as a complete contemporary organization chart. [s2]\n\nThis matters when choosing a source: a statement from one ministry cannot automatically establish policy across every institution associated with a broad subject such as education or energy. Readers should identify the named portfolio and the document's date before interpreting its institutional scope.",
