        "id": "institutional-map",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "An elected chamber within a wider system",
        "content": "The Islamic Consultative Assembly, commonly called the Majles, is Iran's elected legislative chamber. The constitution permits it to legislate within constitutional limits, while assigning review for compatibility with the constitution and Islamic criteria to the Guardian Council. The Expediency Council addresses specified legislative disagreements between these institutions. A parliamentary vote therefore needs to be distinguished from completion of the legislative process. [s1]",
